  "claim": "The American art critic met the painter who produced Life (sculpture). The critic died after the death of Agatha Christie.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Clement Greenberg. Sentence: Clement Greenberg ( ), occasionally writing under the pseudonym K. Hardesh (January 16, 1909 – May 7, 1994), was an American essayist known mainly as an influential visual art critic closely associated with American Modern art of the mid-20th century.\nPage: Agatha Christie. Sentence: Dame Agatha Mary Clarissa Christie, Lady Mallowan, DBE (\"née\" Miller; 15 September 1890 – 12 January 1976) was an English crime novelist, short story writer and playwright.\nPage: Joseph Drapell. Sentence: At the Cranbrook Academy he met visiting Canadian artist Jack Bush and the American art critic Clement Greenberg, who influenced his work.\nPage: Life (sculpture). Sentence: It was commissioned in 1968 by Ben's Bakery and produced by painter Joseph Drapell.",
